erywhere: **default budget** = shap's m = 2d+2048 coalitions (keeps its name). **Headline setting** = the shap Kernel explainer at the default budget wit\n\n  - **Floor b by B (K independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`; rev 11: all 20 model × dataset cells delivered, no pending rows):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.45, B50 0.59, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.77. So the background-draw part shrinks with B, and a part of \n\n- rev 11: floor-b-by-B block refreshed to the 20-cell delivery (b51b17e): medians 0.45/0.59/0.75/0.77; paired difference counts per estimator; no pending rows (experiment-repo, story-repo#7).\n\n- rev 8 (`analysis`'s answers on experiment-repo#5): floor b by B (0.46/0.62/0.75, k-means 0.72), co-headline restricted to shap default at B=50 (mixed against paired Kernel); M5 supported for permutation, unresolved elsewhere; margin table replaces my mean-P_c reading; R1 saving 20–23% at d ≥ 16 wi\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "0ec784d9-8ec3-5caa-9189-b698e933bb76", "at": 1795654985.1211817, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 94834, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "b946a677f38d978a72476b9f578de3e2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "468879fa-2912-5bdf-aa7f-b832c6dfeb56", "at": 1795654985.123294, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 94835, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "b946a677f38d978a72476b9f578de3e2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "06e028cc-6cd2-5285-b688-aed6d81dc395", "at": 1795654985.1253023, "clock": "host", "stream": "r